! lararium-browser Deletion Map

Live inventory of every known sovereignty shore, web2 smell, and page-singleton residue
touching the browser vessel surface. Four classifications:

| Class | Meaning |
|---|---|
| ''Constitutional'' | Belongs in the browser vessel as-is. Satisfies BV-1–BV-7. Migrate freely. |
| ''Adapter'' | DOM or page-global dependency that must stay, but behind one named adapter boundary. Cannot cross worker-side. |
| ''Quarantine'' | Currently carries a mix of constitutional and residue. Needs split before migration. |
| ''Dead residue'' | Whole-page singleton or web2 smell. Delete after new path proves itself. |

<<~ ahu #/shore-inventory>>

!! Shore Inventory

!!! packages/lararium-tw5/src/tw5-browser-surface.ts

| Shore | Line | Class | Note |
|---|---|---|---|
| `mountPanel(engine, container: HTMLElement)` | 38 | Quarantine | Function signature is correct (host calls it). Body couples `window.document`, `shadowRoot`, and `$:/core/ui/RootTemplate`. Body needs rewrite; signature survives as the adapter entry point. |
| `container.attachShadow({ mode: "open" })` | 41 | Adapter | Shadow DOM is a host-side concern. Stays in the projection adapter layer. Never crosses the worker boundary. |
| `document.createElement("style")` | 53 | Adapter | Stylesheet injection is host-side. Stays in adapter. |
| `document.createElement("div")` | 69 | Adapter | DOM construction is host-side. Stays in adapter. |
| `$:/core/ui/RootTemplate` | 76 | Dead residue | Whole-page sovereignty assumption. Replaced by Lararium root contract in S4/S8. The transclude call survives only inside a compatibility shim if S8 determines one is still necessary. |
| `tw.rootWidget.domNodes = [inner]` | 93 | Adapter | TW5 internal event dispatch requires a root domNode. Stays in adapter, explicitly documented as TW5-internal plumbing. |
| `setPalette(engine, paletteName)` | 104 | Constitutional | Writes a tiddler into the wiki. No DOM dependency. Migrate as-is to `@lararium/browser` projection helpers. |
| `setBootSplash(engine, active)` | 115 | Constitutional | Writes/deletes a state tiddler. No DOM dependency. Migrate as-is. |

!!! packages/lararium-tw5/src/index.ts

| Export | Class | Note |
|---|---|---|
| `mountPanel` | Quarantine | Re-exported from the `tw5-browser-surface.ts` module. Should eventually export only the rewritten adapter version. |
| `setPalette` | Constitutional | Fine to re-export from `@lararium/browser` instead; `@lararium/tw5` can keep it as isomorphic helper. |
| `setBootSplash` | Constitutional | Same as `setPalette`. |
| `mountCamera`, `CameraMount` | Constitutional | Isomorphic. No DOM dependency. Central to the projection contract. |

!!! packages/lararium-tw5/src/tw5-vm.ts

| Shore | Class | Note |
|---|---|---|
| `TW5Engine.$tw` | Constitutional | The engine object itself is isomorphic. No DOM types inside. |
| `TW5Engine.fakeDocument` | Constitutional | `TW5FakeDocument` — fake DOM for TW5 filter/render work. Not a real browser document. Stays in `@lararium/tw5`. |
| `TW5Engine.rootWidget` | Constitutional | Isomorphic TW5 widget root. No `HTMLElement` dependency. |
| `mountPanel → tw5-browser-surface.ts` (comment) | Constitutional | The split already happened. The comment correctly names the boundary. |

!!! packages/lararium-mesh/src/vm-pool.ts

| Shore | Class | Note |
|---|---|---|
| `VmPool<T>` | Constitutional | Isomorphic. Already generic. The `BrowserAuthorityPool` in `@lararium/browser` extends or wraps this — does not replace it. |

!!! packages/lararium-tw5/src/tw5-worker-proxy.ts

| Shore | Class | Note |
|---|---|---|
| `AnyWorker` type | Constitutional | Already platform-agnostic. Handles both Node `Worker` and browser `Web Worker` message APIs. |
| `TW5WorkerProxy` | Constitutional | Already designed for browser use. Core of S2 worker boot. Migrates to `@lararium/browser` as the browser worker runtime; `@lararium/tw5` keeps it as the shared proxy class. |
| `WorkerFactory` type | Constitutional | Caller supplies the island constructor. Browser factory goes in `@lararium/browser`; node factory stays in `@lararium/node`. |

!!! No source files yet in packages/lararium-browser/

The package directory exists and is empty. All new source files start here; no legacy code carries into it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/adapter-boundary>>

!! Named Adapter Boundary

All surviving DOM/page references collect in one named file: `tw5-browser-surface.ts` (in `@lararium/tw5`).

This file remains the ''one adapter boundary'' that contains all remaining RootTemplate and DOM compromises.
Every entry in the Adapter class above must route through this file.
No other file in the browser vessel path may import from `window`, `document`, or `HTMLElement` without an explicit migration entry here.

Future HUD surfaces (canvas, UE, Mudlet) bypass this file entirely — they use the island authority's projection interface directly.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/migration-log>>

!! Migration Log

Entries here record what moved, when, and which cheap-check it satisfied.
Empty until S1 lands.

| Sprint | Code moved | From | To | Cheap check satisfied |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| S1 | `BrowserAuthorityId`, `BrowserAuthorityPhase`, `BrowserAuthorityBootParams`, `BrowserAuthorityCapabilities`, `BrowserAuthorityLease`, `BrowserProjectionSnapshot`, `BrowserAuthorityDebugStats`, `BrowserAuthorityReceipt`, `BrowserAuthorityPool` | (new — authored in `@lararium/mesh`) | `packages/lararium-mesh/src/browser-dock.ts` | Law test ✓ (zero DOM types); typecheck ✓ all packages |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/deletion-targets>>

!! Deletion Targets

Delete or quarantine these patterns. Each deletion happens after the replacement proves itself clean.

| Pattern | Why | Replacement | Delete when |
|---|---|---|---|
| `$:/core/ui/RootTemplate` in `mountPanel` body | Whole-page sovereignty assumption | Lararium root contract (S4/S8) | S8 passes all projection adapter tests |
| `document.createElement(...)` outside the named adapter boundary | Any occurrence outside `tw5-browser-surface.ts` indicates a DOM shore that escaped the boundary | Route through adapter or project into worker's fakeDocument | Immediately on discovery |
| `window.$tw` (not currently present; guard against reintroduction) | Page-global authority root | Island authority via `TW5WorkerProxy` | Never allow in; add lint rule |
| Whole-page wiki boot (any code that runs TW5Engine and then attaches to `document.body` directly) | Not present yet; guard against entry | `openBrowserVessel()` → pool → worker → lease → frame | Block at PR review |
| `tw.rootWidget.domNodes = [...]` assignment outside adapter | Leaks DOM binding into authority layer | Keep in adapter only | S4 projection contract established |

<<~/ahu>>

